      "widgets_values": [
        "# SAM 3.1 Video – Cutout & ID System\n\n## Checkpoint (required)\n- [sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors)\n\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n└── 📂 models/\n    └── 📂 checkpoints/\n        └── sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors\n```\n\n## Modules / Nodes (License)\n- **SAM3_VideoTrack / _TrackPreview / _TrackToMask** – ComfyUI Core (native, from 0.27.0). Meta SAM License, commercial use OK.\n- **CheckpointLoaderSimple / CLIPTextEncode / GetVideoComponents / LoadVideo / JoinImageWithAlpha** – Core.\n- **LayerMask: MaskEdgeUltraDetail V2** – ComfyUI_LayerStyle (MIT). The ViTMatte model (hustvl/vitmatte-small, MIT) downloads automatically on first run. If that fails, place it manually into `ComfyUI/models/vitmatte/` and set `method` to VITMatte(local) (details in the \"ViTMatte Tuning\" node).\n- **Fast Groups Bypasser** – rgthree-comfy (MIT).\n- **VHS_VideoCombine** – VideoHelperSuite (for ProRes/WebM).\n\n## Important\n- rgthree toggles require **VueNodes OFF** (Settings → disable 'Vue Nodes'), otherwise only a single switch is drawn.\n- Match FPS in TrackPreview & VideoCombine to the source.\n- ViTMatte runs **per frame** – compute-intensive on long clips.\n- **Output:** Primarily the **B/W matte** as a PNG sequence (`MaskToImage -> SaveImage`) – in AE/Nuke/Premiere apply it as a luma matte on the original video (full quality). Optionally also an extracted RGBA PNG sequence.\n- No VHS/ProRes needed – pure PNG output. The recipient only needs ComfyUI + checkpoint + LayerStyle + rgthree."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
