      "title": "Object Switches – Operation",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Operation – 2 steps\n\n**Step 1 – see the IDs:** Run the workflow once. `SAM3 Video Track` assigns each detected object a **stable ID** (0,1,2,…) across all frames. In the **ID PREVIEW** node you see the video with the numbers painted on in color – that's where you read off who has which ID.\n\n**Step 2 – cut out:** In the **① Enter IDs** node, enter the desired ID(s):\n- `2` → only person 2 is cut out.\n- `0,2,3` → several objects at once.\n- empty / non-existent ID → empty mask (no error).\n\nThen run again → matte + RGBA are saved.\n\n**Find more objects?** Increase `max_objects` in the track node, adjust the prompt (e.g. `person:6`)."
      ],
      "color": "#243",
      "bgcolor": "#020"
    },
