      "title": "Tracking Parameters",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Tracking parameters (SAM3 Video Track)\n\n1. **detection_threshold** (0.0–1.0, default **0.5**) – this is the **score threshold**. Higher = stricter, only confident hits are tracked. Turn it up if an object in the background is picked up by mistake.\n2. **max_objects** (0–64, default **8**) – max. objects tracked simultaneously. `0` = internal cap of 64.\n3. **detect_interval** (from 1, default **1**) – checks for new objects every N frames. `1` = every frame; higher saves compute time, but new objects are then detected later.\n\n**initial_mask** / **conditioning**: at least one of the two must be provided – here the text prompt (`conditioning`) goes in."
      ],
      "color": "#243b6e",
      "bgcolor": "#1a2a4a"
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        1741.5563574072019,
        570.1527782619953
      ],
      "size": [
        683.3919587039913,
        415.84553573483856
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 8,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "ViTMatte Tuning",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# ViTMatte – fine-tuning\n\n**Node:** LayerMask: MaskEdgeUltraDetail V2 (ComfyUI_LayerStyle)\n\n**All parameters in detail:**\n- `method`: **VITMatte** (downloads the model automatically from HuggingFace on first run) / **VITMatte(local)** (uses the already downloaded model, no internet access needed anymore – switch to this afterwards!) / PyMatting / GuidedFilter\n- `mask_grow`: expands the mask before detail processing (currently **1**)\n- `fix_gap`: closes small holes/gaps in the mask edge (currently **4**, 4–8 sensible)\n- `fix_threshold`: threshold for the hole repair – higher = more aggressive (currently **0.75**)\n- `edge_erode` / `edge_dilate`: pull the edge inward/outward – **8/12** for hair/fine edges (default would be 6/6)\n- `black_point`: high (**0.83**) → against ghost haze/residual shadows in the background\n- `white_point`: **0.99** → how \"fully opaque\" the foreground is treated as\n- `device`: cuda\n- `max_megapixels`: **4.0+** for high resolution (RTX 5090)\n\n**Model download:** hustvl/vitmatte-small (MIT), normally downloads automatically. If the auto-download fails (firewall/proxy/no internet on the workstation), download manually and place under:\n```\n📂 ComfyUI/\n└── 📂 models/\n    └── 📂 vitmatte/\n        └── (all files from hustvl/vitmatte-small)\n```\nThen set `method` to **VITMatte(local)**.\n\n⚠️ **Memory warning:** For frames above 2K resolution ViTMatte eats a lot of VRAM/RAM. If it crashes/hangs: downscale the video to 1080p or similar beforehand, or lower `max_megapixels`."
      ],
      "color": "#323",
      "bgcolor": "#535"
    },
